Check: check_listeningprocs

Neither ss nor lsof was found, so the listening processes were read with
netstat. It gives less: the process name is cut from its command line
(an "avahi-daemon: r" rather than "avahi-daemon"), so the findings can
differ from a run on a system with ss, and it may not be able to name
the process at all. Installing iproute2, which provides ss, avoids this.
or the user that runs it.
